            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_29d62570">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_id36139ddb">Niels W. Gade</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_34ea6f80">Carl Schultes</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_idaa47fbc8">
               <date isodate="1848-04" xml:id="date_157c06a8">Apr. 1848</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_idcd129413">Leipzig</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id51ec7dc7">
               <p xml:id="idm185">Gade met Carl Schultes in Leipzig at the end of 1847. At that time Gade had written music for five of the six poems in the latter's "Sechs Reiterlieder". However, Gade asked Schultes to write a new poem instead of the one he had not yet set to music, to end the story. Although Gade had meant the songs to be an integrated cycle, they were probably never performed as such, apart from a performance in Bielefeld during the concert season 1869-1870.</p>
            </history>
